  "ingredients": [
    "2 cups crushed fresh strawberries",
    "4 cups sugar",
    "1 (1.75 ounce) package dry pectin",
    "0.75 cup water"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Gather all ingredients.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/nt8Cl8ucMOLBzknNy2OSzb8w-lI=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/51835-strawberry-freezer-jam-ddmfs-5482-01-3x4-dd12c0c37fcb4cacadb064f1b51594de.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/51835/step_01.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Crush strawberries using a potato masher in a large bowl. (Alternatively, pulse strawberries in a food processor until just finely chopped but not pureed.) Drain strawberries through a fine mesh strainer; reserve juice for another use. Transfer 2 cups crushed strawberries to a large bowl (reserve any extra strawberries for another use); add sugar, and stir until evenly combined. Let stand at room temperature for 10 minutes, stirring occasionally.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/_pBbmmnjRrDl26M72Yh8YjYRDKs=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/51835-strawberry-freezer-jam-ddmfs-5489-02-3x4-c3edd6c713de4f5f8a46f71bb703effe.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/51835/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Meanwhile, stir pectin and water together in a small saucepan until combined. Bring to a boil over medium-high heat; boil, stirring constantly, until a thick paste forms and pectin is fully dissolved, about 2 minutes.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/rTfdn3l1EYzKG23hAhWLDWXWknI=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/51835-strawberry-freezer-jam-ddmfs-5496-03-3x4-ea7e6e0717e741f084c7dcc45bacb20c.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/51835/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Stir boiling pectin-water mixture into strawberry mixture in large bowl; stir constantly for 3 minutes. To check if jam is set, coat back of a spoon with jam; run a finger through it. If jam remains separated, it is properly set. If jam runs back together, it is not set; stir until set, 3 more minutes. Pour into 2 sterilized pint-size jars or other storage containers, leaving a 1/2-inch space at the top to allow for expansion. Place tops on containers, and leave at room temperature for 24 hours.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/f-fMrfMuqEzziagv2XWPt0jf6fI=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/51835-strawberry-freezer-jam-ddmfs-5503-04-3x4-3698a7302fb949ff99d8a3c335a450c9.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/51835/step_04.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Place in refrigerator for at least 1 hour before serving, or freeze until ready to use or up to 3 months. Enjoy!",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/qEt0COKM6fpeRWlsD8rGFSu9wWs=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/51835-strawberry-freezer-jam-ddmfs-5627-hero-3x4-70eaf3112e7f48b6959cc0bc565dbdb1.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/51835/step_05.webp"
    }
  ],
